  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data view:** `Kibana Sample Data Logs` (`kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`). The fields I used are `response.keyword` (status code, stored as a string), `bytes`, and `timestamp`.\n\n**Dashboard: \"EFF-c3d9b986 Web logs overview\"**\n- Total requests (metric, count)\n- Average response size in bytes (metric, average of `bytes`)\n- Requests over time (line, date histogram on `timestamp`)\n- Requests by response code (bar, terms on `response.keyword`)\n- 5xx responses (ES|QL metric: `FROM kibana_sample_data_logs | WHERE response.keyword LIKE \"5*\" | STATS errors = COUNT(*)`)\n\nI set the dashboard's time range to the last year, because I don't know when the sample data was loaded. Narrow it if you want.\n\n**Alert rule: \"EFF-c3d9b986 5xx spike\"** (id `2b42887b-08a8-49b0-8a43-c2fea942b16b`)\n- Type `.es-query`, consumer `stackAlerts`, runs every 1m, enabled\n- Query: `response.keyword` wildcard `5*` on `kibana_sample_data_logs`\n- Fires when the count is greater than 10 over a 5-minute window\n- It has no action connector, because none exist yet. It will show alerts in the Kibana UI but won't notify anyone. I can add a connector and attach it if you want notifications.\n\n**Things I didn't verify:**\n- I couldn't query the data directly. `KIBANA_TEST_API_KEY` is empty in my shell, so REST calls return 401. I used the MCP Kibana tools instead, which don't return query results. So I haven't confirmed the response-code values or that the 5xx panel and rule return non-zero counts. The `5*` wildcard assumes the codes are stored as plain strings like `503`.\n- The rule's status was still `pending` when I checked, so I haven't seen it run yet.",
